   "text": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1\">.mw-parser-output .hatnote{font-style:italic}</style><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">For the gadget version, see <a href=\"/wiki/Gadget_theorem\" title=\"Gadget theorem\">Gadget theorem</a>.</div>\n<table class=\"infobox\"><tbody><tr><th>Field</th><td>Widget theory</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p>Infobox paragraph with <b>bold</b> that is not a definition.</p></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>In <a href=\"/wiki/Widget_theory\" title=\"Widget theory\">widget theory</a>, the <b>widget lemma</b> states that every finite widget <span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\" style=\"display: none;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle G}\"><semantics><mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>G</mi></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle G}</annotation></semantics></math></span><img src=\"https://wikimedia.invalid/inline.svg\" class=\"mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert\" aria-hidden=\"true\" alt=\"{\\displaystyle G}\"></span> has a spanning gadget.<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> It is named after a fictional author&#160;&amp; friends.\n</p>\n<meta property=\"mw:PageProp/toc\" />\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Statement\">Statement</h2></div>\n<p>Let <span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\" style=\"display: none;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle G}\"><semantics><mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>G</mi></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle G}</annotation></semantics></math></span><img src=\"https://wikimedia.invalid/inline.svg\" class=\"mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert\" aria-hidden=\"true\" alt=\"{\\displaystyle G}\"></span> be a finite widget of order <span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\" style=\"display: none;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle n}\"><semantics><mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>n</mi></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle n}</annotation></semantics></math></span><img src=\"https://wikimedia.invalid/inline.svg\" class=\"mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert\" aria-hidden=\"true\" alt=\"{\\displaystyle n}\"></span>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"math_theorem\" style=\"margin:1em 2em\"><strong class=\"theorem-name\">Widget lemma</strong>&#160;&mdash;&#32;Every finite widget <span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\" style=\"display: none;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle G}\"><semantics><mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>G</mi></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle G}</annotation></semantics></math></span><img src=\"https://wikimedia.invalid/inline.svg\" class=\"mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert\" aria-hidden=\"true\" alt=\"{\\displaystyle G}\"></span> of order <span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\" style=\"display: none;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle n}\"><semantics><mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>n</mi></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle n}</annotation></semantics></math></span><img src=\"https://wikimedia.invalid/inline.svg\" class=\"mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert\" aria-hidden=\"true\" alt=\"{\\displaystyle n}\"></span> has a spanning gadget whose size divides <span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\" style=\"display: none;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle n}\"><semantics><mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>n</mi></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle n}</annotation></semantics></math></span><img src=\"https://wikimedia.invalid/inline.svg\" class=\"mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert\" aria-hidden=\"true\" alt=\"{\\displaystyle n}\"></span>.</div>\n<dl><dd><span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-block\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-block mwe-math-mathml-a11y\" style=\"display: none;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle |S| \\mid n}\"><semantics><mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>|</mi></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle |S| \\mid n}</annotation></semantics></math></span><img src=\"https://wikimedia.invalid/block.svg\" class=\"mwe-math-fallback-image-block mw-invert skin-invert\" aria-hidden=\"true\" alt=\"{\\displaystyle |S| \\mid n}\"></span></dd></dl>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Corollaries\">Corollaries</h3></div>\n<ul><li>Every two spanning gadgets of <span class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><span class=\"mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y\" style=\"display: none;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"{\\displaystyle G}\"><semantics><mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>G</mi></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">{\\displaystyle G}</annotation></semantics></math></span><img src=\"https://wikimedia.invalid/inline.svg\" class=\"mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert\" aria-hidden=\"true\" alt=\"{\\displaystyle G}\"></span> are conjugate.</li><li>A <b>prime widget</b> has exactly one spanning gadget.</li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"See_also\">See also</h2></div>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Sprocket\">Sprocket</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"References\">References</h2></div>\n<div class=\"reflist\"><div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"cite_note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">A. Author, <i>Widgets</i>, a fictional book.</span></li></ol></div></div>\n<div class=\"navbox\"><table><tr><th>Widget theory</th><td><a href=\"/wiki/Widget_lemma\">Widget lemma</a> &#8226; <a href=\"/wiki/Gadget_theorem\">Gadget theorem</a></td></tr></table></div>\n<!-- NewPP limit report would be here without disablelimitreport -->\n</div>",
   "title": "Widget lemma"
  }
